{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) has assigned stitch task #5446 to implement srd067-split R3.1-R3.4 in the go-unix-utils project. These requirements add suffix control and additional options to the `cmd/split` utility:\n   - **R3.1**: `-a N` or `--suffix-length=N` — configurable suffix length (default 2)\n   - **R3.2**: `-d` or `--numeric-suffixes` — use numeric suffixes (00, 01, ...) instead of alphabetic (aa, ab, ...)\n   - **R3.3**: `--additional-suffix=SUFFIX` — append extra suffix to each output filename\n   - **R3.4**: `--filter=COMMAND` — pipe each piece to a shell command with `$FILE` available as the output filename\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/split/main.go` and `cmd/split/split_test.go`. Acceptance criteria require compilation, all tests pass (including existing R1/R2 tests), go vet clean, and each R3.x covered by at least one differential test.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing against GNU `gsplit` reference binary via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - Manual flag parsing (no cobra in cmd/ utilities)\n   - `pkg/sizeparse` for byte count parsing with unit suffixes\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for SIGPIPE handling\n   - Alphabetic suffix generation (a-z base-26 encoding)\n   - `LC_ALL=C` in test environment\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gsplit\")` with `t.Skip` if not found\n   - ExpectedFiles map in DiffTest for verifying output file contents\n   - The `--filter=COMMAND` feature requires piping output through a shell command where `$FILE` is set to the would-be output filename\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd067-split.yaml** (read, full SRD)\n     - Defines R3.1-R3.4 requirements for suffix control and filter\n     - Non-goals: no `--verbose`, no `--elide-empty-files` beyond `-n`\n     - Package imports: `sizeparse` and `sys`\n   \n   - **cmd/split/main.go** (read, to be modified — 541 lines)\n     - Existing implementation covers R1.1-R1.4 (line splitting) and R2.1-R2.4 (byte/chunk splitting)\n     - `options` struct (lines 28-36): has `mode`, `modeSet`, `lines`, `bytesVal`, `lineBytes`, `chunks`, `prefix` — needs `suffixLen`, `numeric`, `additionalSuffix`, `filter` fields\n     - `parseArgs` (line 62): manual arg parsing loop — needs new flag handlers\n     - `parseLongFlag` (line 110): handles `--lines`, `--bytes`, `--line-bytes`, `--number` — needs `--suffix-length`, `--numeric-suffixes`, `--additional-suffix`, `--filter`\n     - `shortFlagSetter` (line 160): maps `l`, `b`, `C`, `n` — needs `a` and `d`\n     - `openPiece` (line 242): creates files with `alphabeticSuffix(index, 2)` — hardcoded length 2, needs to use opts.suffixLen, numeric mode, additional suffix\n     - `alphabeticSuffix` (line 250): generates base-26 suffix — needs numeric counterpart\n     - `run` (line 266): dispatches to split mode functions, passes `opts.prefix` — needs to thread suffix options through\n     - All split functions (`splitLines`, `splitBytes`, `splitLineBytes`, `splitChunks`) call `openPiece` or `writePiece` which calls `openPiece` — the suffix/filter changes need to propagate through these\n\n   - **cmd/split/split_test.go** (read, to be modified — 213 lines)\n     - `TestDiff` function builds binary and looks up `gsplit`\n     - Test groups: `lineSplitTests`, `prefixAndStdinTests`, `byteSplitTests`, `lineByteTests`, `chunkTests`, `conflictTests`\n     - `normalizeCmdErr` normalizer strips command name prefix from error messages\n     - `generateLines(from, to)` helper generates numbered lines\n     - Needs new test groups for: suffix length (-a), numeric suffixes (-d), additional suffix, filter, and combinations\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The task is still in the reading/planning phase.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read all three required files to understand the existing implementation structure\n   - Identified that `openPiece` and suffix generation are the key functions to modify\n   - Identified that all split mode functions use `openPiece`/`writePiece` and will need the suffix options threaded through\n   - The `--filter=COMMAND` feature is the most complex addition — requires `os/exec` to pipe to shell with `$FILE` env var set\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The first (and only) user message is the massive task description containing: role definition, repository file listing, project context (vision, architecture, specs, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements R3.1-R3.4, design decisions, acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Add `suffixLen` (default 2), `numeric` (bool), `additionalSuffix` (string), `filter` (string) fields to the `options` struct\n   - Add flag parsing for `-a N`/`--suffix-length=N`, `-d`/`--numeric-suffixes`, `--additional-suffix=SUFFIX`, `--filter=COMMAND`\n   - Add `numericSuffix(index, length)` function parallel to `alphabeticSuffix`\n   - Refactor `openPiece` to accept suffix options (length, numeric, additional suffix)\n   - Thread suffix options through all split functions (splitLines, splitBytes, splitLineBytes, splitChunks, writePiece)\n   - Implement filter mode: instead of writing to a file, pipe through shell command with `$FILE` env var\n   - Add differential test cases for R3.1 (suffix length), R3.2 (numeric suffixes), R3.3 (additional suffix), R3.4 (filter)\n   - Verify: `go build -o bin/split ./cmd/split/`, `go test ./cmd/split/... -count=1`, `go vet ./cmd/split/...`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three files (SRD, main.go, split_test.go) and was about to begin the implementation phase. I had identified all the changes needed but had not yet written any code. The next step was to plan the full implementation and write all changes before building/testing.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the R3.1-R3.4 changes in `cmd/split/main.go` — specifically:\n   1. Add new fields to `options` struct\n   2. Add flag parsing for `-a`, `-d`, `--suffix-length`, `--numeric-suffixes`, `--additional-suffix`, `--filter`\n   3. Add `numericSuffix` function and refactor `openPiece`/`writePiece` to use configurable suffix options\n   4. Implement filter mode with shell command piping\n   5. Then add test cases in `cmd/split/split_test.go`\n   6. Then run build/vet/test to verify\n   \n   The task description states: \"Implement srd067-split R3.1 per the SRD specification\", \"Implement srd067-split R3.2 per the SRD specification\", \"Implement srd067-split R3.3 per the SRD specification\", \"Implement srd067-split R3.4 per the SRD specification\" — all in `cmd/split/main.go` with differential tests in `cmd/split/split_test.go`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5446/f0df892c-28a4-4ebb-8b09-6d4534cd0727.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0df892c-28a4-4ebb-8b09-6d4534cd0727","uuid":"4e05a2f0-1381-4a98-bc60-b1d0c156fe50","timestamp":"2026-05-21T19:34:47.320Z","isSynthetic":true}
