n the same working directory (lines 99-100)\n4. **Normalization**: Applies all normalization functions to stdout and stderr of both binaries (lines 101-102)\n5. **Output Comparison**: Compares stdout, stderr, and exit codes (line 103)\n6. **File Validation**: Checks expected files using `checkExpectedFiles()` (line 104)\n\n## ExpectedFiles Handling\n\nThe `checkExpectedFiles` function (lines 211-227):\n- Returns early if `ExpectedFiles` is nil\n- For each file path in the map, constructs the full path by joining WorkDir with the relative path\n- Reads the actual file from the working directory\n- Compares the actual contents byte-for-byte with the expected contents\n- Fails the test if any file is missing or contents don't match exactly\n\n**File location**: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5446/pkg/testutils/difftest.go`"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0df892c-28a4-4ebb-8b09-6d4534cd0727","uuid":"cf1dd045-ee83-404b-9ce4-2bf9fb23d7e4","timestamp":"2026-05-21T19:35:11.941Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5446/pkg/testutils/, find the DiffTest struct definition and the RunDiffTests function. I need to understand:\n1. What fields DiffTest has (especially any Env field for environment variables, and any field for checking output files)\n2. How RunDiffTests works — does it run in a temp directory? How does it compare output files?\n3. Is there an ExpectedFiles field or similar?\n\nSearch breadth: medium","agentId":"ab2004d79cc4afb4b","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information you need. Here's a comprehensive analysis of the DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests function:\n\n## DiffTest Struct Fields\n\nThe `DiffTest` struct (lines 46-55) has the following fields:\n\n1. **Name** (string) - Identifies the subtest (used with t.Run)\n2. **Args** ([]string) - Command-l